<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav crude oil imports up in August.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav crude oil imports up in August.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yugoslav crude oil imports rose to 71,909 tonnes in August from 59,798 tonnes in July, the Federal Statistics Office said on Monday.</p>
<p>The imports were worth $12 million against $8 million in July.</p>
<p>Imports of refined oil products were 27,635 tonnes, up from 19,483 tonnes in July.</p>
<p>Cumulative Jan-Aug crude imports stood at 306,031 tonnes and were valued at $49 million. Oil product imports totalled 861,865 tonnes, worth $184 million.</p>
<p>-- Gordana Kukic, Belgrade Newsroom +381 11 222 4254</p>
